From 6ca35480d0a5b98ca102caae60171ee970e71bba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:15:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] navi-prime, navi-high-yield: add vault fees and revenue

Fees adapters for NAVI's navi_vault product on Sui, split into the two
Prime (blue-chip) vaults and the two High Yield vaults to match the TVL
listings.

dailyFees is the gross yield the vaults earn from the NAVI lending
markets they supply into; dailyRevenue is the management and performance
fee NAVI takes on it; dailySupplySideRevenue is the remainder that goes
to depositors, so dailyFees = dailyRevenue + dailySupplySideRevenue.
Fee rates are not hardcoded - the amounts come from NAVI's accounting.

DO NOT MERGE YET. Both adapters read a `vaults` section that NAVI's
DefiLlama fee endpoint does not serve today; the live endpoint covers
the lending market only. The adapters throw until NAVI ships that field,
which is deliberate rather than returning a zero the refill job would
cache.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
